    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0739" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2240: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-24T15:00:00+01:00">July 24, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 24—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>644. With regard to the situation in Spain, we were informed at the Foreign
                    Office this morning that the French Government has one destroyer off San
                    Sebastián, one on the north coast to evacuate French nationals from Bilbao and
                    Santander, a cruiser stationed at Barcelona, a destroyer on the east coast
                    between Maka and Valencia and a small destroyer will attempt to go up the river
                    to Seville. It was stated that these ships will all endeavor to evacuate French
                    nationals wherever this seems advisable and that they would of course take on
                    board any Americans who desire to make use of these facilities.<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d598-f1"/></p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s 245, July 23, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="59" xml:id="d598-f2"/>
                    appropriate instructions are being sent to the French authorities at
                    Marseille.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Straus</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d598-f1" n="58" xml:id="d598-f1-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 249, July 24, 5 p.m., the Secretary of State instructed the
                    Ambassador to inform the Foreign Office of his deep appreciation of the offer of
                    the French Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d598-f2" n="59" xml:id="d598-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it instructed the Ambassador to take up with the French authorities
                    the question of making provision for the landing at Marseille of such Americans
                    as might be evacuated from Spain (852.00/2209).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
